  1| /**
  2|  * src/auth.ts — Native TypeScript Meta API authentication pipeline.
  3|  *
  4|  * Replaces the Rust binary (`$PREFIX/lib/muse/muse`) `login` flow with a
  5|  * pure-TypeScript OAuth 2.0 Device Authorization Grant (RFC 8628) client.
  6|  *
  7|  * Evidence-grounded against the shipped Rust binary:
  8|  * - default OAuth base:            https://auth.meta.com
  9|  * - default Model API base:        https://api.meta.ai/v1
 10|  * - device auth endpoint (suffix): /oidc/device/authorization/
 11|  * - device token endpoint (suffix):/oidc/device/token/
 12|  * - grant: urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:device_code
 13|  * - registration client_name:      "Muse Code"
 14|  * - discovery: .well-known/oauth-protected-resource,
 15|  *              .well-known/oauth-authorization-server,
 16|  *              .well-known/openid-configuration
 17|  * - TokenResponse: access_token, token_type, expires_in, refresh_token, scope
 18|  * - MintedKey: api_key, require_payment, action_url, user_*, subs_*
 19|  * - auth.json schema: { schema_version: 1,
 20|  *     providers: { meta: { access_token, refresh_token?, expires_at?,
 21|  *       obtained_via, api_key, api_base_url, user_full_name, user_email,
 22|  *       user_avatar_url?, mechanism, record_version?, server_name?,
 23|  *       resource_url_sha256?, issuer?, client_id?, registered_redirect_uri? } } }
 24|  * - META_API_KEY env always takes priority over account login.
 25|  *
 26|  * NodeOS compliance:
 27|  * - Zero hardcoded workspace directories. Credentials live in XDG config
 28|  *   (`$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/muse/auth.json` or `~/.config/muse/auth.json`) for
 29|  *   byte-compat with the Rust binary. NodeOS CWD-bound artifacts
 30|  *   (agy_nodeos.db, workflow.json, daemon.log) are NOT touched here; they
 31|  *   are handled by src/index.ts `init` and src/tui.ts sessions.
 32|  *
 33|  * Transport: global fetch (Node >= 18) with timeout + 1 MiB OAuth size bound.
 34|  */
